  'Interfax and TASS in English, citing the Russian Defence Ministry, report that overnight drones hit four ships carrying military and dual-use cargo for the Ukrainian army, three bulk carriers in the port of Reni, where port infrastructure was also hit, and one ship en route to Odesa, as well as logistics facilities in Khmelnytskyi and Kovel. In the afternoon RIA Novosti and Interfax relayed a new ministry statement: a container ship delivering cargo for the Ukrainian army to the port of Odesa was hit at sea.',
  'Suspilne, citing Reuters, reports that after a meeting of the North Atlantic Council on Black Sea security NATO will step up its presence in the region and send teams of specialists for forensic analysis of explosives from incident sites; alliance spokeswoman Allison Hart speaks of additional surveillance, reconnaissance and forensic assets. The outlet recalls an attack by Russian drones on a civilian merchant ship carrying corn in neutral waters, in which the captain was killed. The report says nothing about the strikes on ships in Reni claimed by the Russian Defence Ministry.',
